WEBVTT

00:01:43.984 --> 00:01:46.919
So we're in the middle
of nowhere with nothing?

00:01:52.893 --> 00:01:54.485
What is this?

00:01:55.295 --> 00:01:58.331
Sorry. No more snacks for a while.

00:01:58.331 --> 00:02:00.767
We're almost out of food.

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:06.228
I see. We'll have to ask Kiyone to stop
and do some grocery shopping, I guess.

00:02:12.546 --> 00:02:14.173
What's going on?

00:02:20.053 --> 00:02:22.722
Oh, my. I wonder what's going on.

00:02:22.722 --> 00:02:24.424
How can you be so unaware?

00:02:24.424 --> 00:02:27.727
Engine power's now going down to 50, 40...

00:02:27.727 --> 00:02:29.496
- Well, what's the matter?
- Shut up!

00:02:29.496 --> 00:02:32.165
Hey, what are you doing in here?

00:02:32.165 --> 00:02:34.367
It sounds like the engine's
about to stop, you guys.

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:37.070
I know that! I'm working on it right now!

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:40.073
Kiyone, I told you, you should learn to relax.

00:02:40.073 --> 00:02:42.268
And you should learn to panic...

00:02:56.223 --> 00:02:58.248
Oh... it's broken.

00:03:19.412 --> 00:03:22.015
Right. You want me to fix this.

00:03:22.015 --> 00:03:23.717
Yup.

00:03:23.717 --> 00:03:25.852
- Me, fix this?
- Mm-hmm.

00:03:25.852 --> 00:03:29.623
Let me make this clear for you:
I'm a scientist, not a mechanic.

00:03:29.623 --> 00:03:31.791
Now I have some research
to do, so if you'll excuse me...

00:03:31.791 --> 00:03:33.460
Oh, wait, Washu...

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:37.397
I mean, Professor Washu the
greatest scientist in the universe.

00:03:37.397 --> 00:03:38.431
I know you can do it.

00:03:38.431 --> 00:03:42.335
Yes, you're a genius, and
I agree with Kiyone, Washu.

00:03:42.335 --> 00:03:46.172
The greatest genius in the
universe should be able to do this.

00:03:46.172 --> 00:03:50.277
Since you put it that way fixing
engine trouble should be a piece of cake.

00:03:50.277 --> 00:03:52.345
We thought so.

00:03:52.345 --> 00:03:55.371
It's a piece of cake for you.

00:03:56.216 --> 00:03:58.411
It's no big deal for a genius.

00:04:00.587 --> 00:04:03.290
Washu, you are a genius.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:05.690
Washu, you are the greatest in the universe.

00:04:08.762 --> 00:04:10.630
Thank God she's so easy to please.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:11.756
No kidding.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.631
Hey, be quiet, will ya?

00:04:16.236 --> 00:04:18.397
Aha, here they are. I've got them.

00:04:24.578 --> 00:04:27.138
Hello? Anybody in there?

00:04:36.222 --> 00:04:40.921
Okay, I'm gonna use an S-32 plug here.

00:04:42.162 --> 00:04:44.631
Now I need some adhesive.

00:04:44.631 --> 00:04:48.435
Where is that adhesive?
Where are you, adhesive?

00:04:48.435 --> 00:04:51.371
- Is this what you need?
- Oh, thank you.

00:04:51.371 --> 00:04:54.306
I just stabilize this, and then...

00:04:58.912 --> 00:05:02.248
Maybe this is what she should have used.

00:05:02.248 --> 00:05:04.910
I don't know. What do you think, Washu?

00:05:06.853 --> 00:05:08.684
You get out of here.

00:05:17.831 --> 00:05:20.500
J-Just what does this mean?

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:23.162
What's going on here, huh?

00:05:25.605 --> 00:05:27.095
Huh?

00:05:32.979 --> 00:05:35.504
Have you been stealing our food?

00:05:38.585 --> 00:05:41.087
Idiot. Why are you carrying that around?

00:05:41.087 --> 00:05:43.920
I told you to eat them in private.

00:05:44.557 --> 00:05:46.388
Just as I thought!

00:05:47.661 --> 00:05:50.563
So you're behind all of this, aren't you?

00:05:50.563 --> 00:05:54.334
So what if I am? It's only a
little food. Don't be so uptight.

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:56.036
You don't even feel guilty!

00:05:56.036 --> 00:05:58.872
Don't frown too much, or those
wrinkles will never disappear.

00:05:58.872 --> 00:06:00.974
How dare you say that?

00:06:00.974 --> 00:06:04.678
Now, let's calm down,
both of you. What's gone is gone.

00:06:04.678 --> 00:06:06.513
We need to go to the grocery store.

00:06:06.513 --> 00:06:09.049
But how? The ship is stalled, Grandpa.

00:06:09.049 --> 00:06:10.750
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.344
Well, I'll go. Is that what you want?

00:06:14.688 --> 00:06:16.556
It seems only proper.

00:06:16.556 --> 00:06:18.158
- Okay!
- Huh?

00:06:18.158 --> 00:06:20.524
I'll go. Money, please.

00:06:21.361 --> 00:06:24.898
I suppose you do need some money. Here.

00:06:24.898 --> 00:06:26.399
Right.

00:06:26.399 --> 00:06:28.234
What?!

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:31.638
Now... let's go, Tenchi.

00:06:31.638 --> 00:06:34.474
Uh, now wait a minute. Tenchi can't go.

00:06:34.474 --> 00:06:36.276
We need all the hands we
can get to fix the engine trouble.

00:06:36.276 --> 00:06:38.311
We have a lot of things to do.

00:06:38.311 --> 00:06:41.542
- Right, Tenchi?
- Uh, yeah.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.652
I could come along.

00:06:45.652 --> 00:06:47.916
I'm outta here. See ya.

00:06:54.761 --> 00:06:59.699
Tenchi, do you think Ryoko is
going to be okay all by herself?

00:06:59.699 --> 00:07:02.293
I think she's going to be just fine.

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:10.107
She brought it on herself.
She has to face the music.

00:07:13.413 --> 00:07:15.915
There. It's all done.

00:07:15.915 --> 00:07:18.418
Now that this is complete,
all I have to do next is...

00:07:18.418 --> 00:07:21.046
Ok, switch on!

00:07:27.427 --> 00:07:30.362
Looks like a few extra days
till the repairs are finished.

00:07:31.731 --> 00:07:36.069
Ryoko should be back anytime now, right?

00:07:36.069 --> 00:07:39.672
Yeah, anytime now.

00:07:39.672 --> 00:07:43.643
I hope she's not spending
our money on something else.

00:07:43.643 --> 00:07:46.579
You worry too much, Ayeka.

00:07:46.579 --> 00:07:49.139
Let's try to trust her. Come on.

00:07:58.091 --> 00:08:00.560
Another <i>sake,</i> please.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:02.529
What? Another one?

00:08:02.529 --> 00:08:04.798
You shouldn't drink so much, you know.

00:08:04.798 --> 00:08:08.401
Don't worry. I'm fine,
and I've got a lot of money.

00:08:08.401 --> 00:08:10.266
Well, if you insist.

00:08:14.641 --> 00:08:16.404
What's wrong?

00:08:18.611 --> 00:08:20.413
Don't worry about those guys.

00:08:20.413 --> 00:08:21.080
Here we go.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.148
Thanks so much.

00:08:22.148 --> 00:08:27.687
Hey, even if we're a little late, it'll be fine.

00:08:27.687 --> 00:08:30.679
Now, why don't you
join me? Here, have some.

00:08:39.632 --> 00:08:43.503
Ryo-Ohki, that's it.
Now you're getting into the spirit.

00:08:43.503 --> 00:08:45.705
All right then, let's hit it!

00:08:45.705 --> 00:08:49.475
Yeah! Yeah! Hah! Yeah!

00:08:49.475 --> 00:08:52.412
All right! Yeah! Yeah! Yeah, yeah!

00:08:52.412 --> 00:08:54.607
Party down!

00:08:57.116 --> 00:09:00.753
She comes back...
She comes back not.

00:09:00.753 --> 00:09:03.122
Comes back, comes back not...

00:09:03.122 --> 00:09:04.090
- Mihoshi, you are aware of the fact
- Comes back...

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:05.258
- Mihoshi, you are aware of the fact
- Comes back not...

00:09:05.258 --> 00:09:06.793
- that you are the cause
of this delay, are you not?
- Comes back...

00:09:06.793 --> 00:09:07.827
- that you are the cause
of this delay, are you not?
- Comes back not...

00:09:07.827 --> 00:09:08.995
- Listen, I don't want you in
that engine room anymore.
- Comes back...

00:09:08.995 --> 00:09:10.396
- Listen, I don't want you in
that engine room anymore.
- Comes back not...

00:09:10.396 --> 00:09:12.198
- Listen, I don't want you in
that engine room anymore.
- Comes back...

00:09:12.198 --> 00:09:14.133
Uh, Kiyone?

00:09:14.133 --> 00:09:16.931
Hey, I'm not really that...

00:09:19.138 --> 00:09:19.906
Oh...

00:09:19.906 --> 00:09:23.276
- Wh-What now?
- Wow! Here, look, Kiyone.

00:09:23.276 --> 00:09:27.113
This flower tells me Ryoko is
coming back, and it won't be long.

00:09:27.113 --> 00:09:30.083
Let's try to hang in there, okay, Kiyone?

00:09:30.083 --> 00:09:33.853
- Mihoshi?
- I'm starving.

00:09:33.853 --> 00:09:35.582
Mihoshi!

00:09:37.023 --> 00:09:39.859
Mihoshi, what are you doing?

00:09:39.859 --> 00:09:44.387
Ryoko, please come back
to us soon. We're starving.

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:05.385
All right!

00:10:05.385 --> 00:10:08.321
Hey, somebody, bring me some big buckets!

00:10:08.321 --> 00:10:10.915
Large buckets coming right up.

00:10:13.927 --> 00:10:17.864
Congratulations to the lady on 327!
You've just hit the jackpot!

00:10:17.864 --> 00:10:20.800
Win more coins than
you can carry, everybody!

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.870
Here's our special limited-time offer!

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:25.305
Double odds!

00:10:25.305 --> 00:10:27.364
Double odds on all slot machines!

00:10:50.063 --> 00:10:51.998
Hello, everyone.

00:10:51.998 --> 00:10:55.501
It's time for more delicious,
delectable delicacies.

00:10:55.501 --> 00:10:58.204
Today's show, we're going to
show you how to cook this dish.

00:10:58.204 --> 00:11:01.799
It looks so good and so
mouthwatering, doesn't it?

00:11:07.246 --> 00:11:09.382
I'm so hungry.

00:11:09.382 --> 00:11:11.751
Yeah.

00:11:11.751 --> 00:11:14.549
Ryoko, where can you be?

00:11:18.825 --> 00:11:20.760
Wow!

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:22.921
I'm gonna dig in.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:30.592
Tastes good!

00:11:32.238 --> 00:11:37.043
This place deserves three stars.
I'll try a five-star next.

00:11:37.043 --> 00:11:42.071
But before I do that, I'd like to
order five jumbo steaks! And hurry!

00:11:52.792 --> 00:11:55.022
Oh, I can't go on like this!

00:11:56.329 --> 00:11:58.765
Washu, hang in there!

00:11:58.765 --> 00:12:01.067
You can do it, Washu!

00:12:01.067 --> 00:12:06.372
Come on, Washu! You can
do it, Washu! Come on, Washu!

00:12:06.372 --> 00:12:09.398
Hey, you guys try fixin' it, why don't ya?

00:12:11.544 --> 00:12:14.172
I'm too hungry for this.

00:12:19.619 --> 00:12:21.109
Wow!

00:12:23.156 --> 00:12:25.283
This looks great.

00:12:33.332 --> 00:12:35.301
Oh, take it easy.

00:12:35.301 --> 00:12:36.632
Look here.

00:12:38.237 --> 00:12:39.672
Now you're happy.

00:12:39.672 --> 00:12:43.403
Okay, bring 'em in!

00:13:19.745 --> 00:13:21.736
<i>Bon appétit!</i>

00:13:30.022 --> 00:13:32.047
That was just great.

00:13:35.628 --> 00:13:38.798
I want food! Give me some food!

00:13:38.798 --> 00:13:41.167
Hey, Dad.

00:13:41.167 --> 00:13:43.803
Get away! Get ahold of yourself!

00:13:43.803 --> 00:13:45.498
Tenchi!

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:52.044
You're flipping out, Dad. What are you
gonna do with that orange peel, anyway?

00:13:52.044 --> 00:13:55.781
It's better than dying of starvation on
this stupid spaceship in the middle of space!

00:13:55.781 --> 00:13:59.148
This rice and curry is delicious!

00:14:01.287 --> 00:14:02.688
This is good.

00:14:02.688 --> 00:14:06.759
Here I see some hamburger steak
and here I see some pasta, too.

00:14:06.759 --> 00:14:10.263
Fried shrimp, stew, tempura...

00:14:10.263 --> 00:14:12.595
So much to eat!

00:14:13.366 --> 00:14:14.200
Mihoshi...

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:17.370
Look, Kiyone, we have so much food...

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:20.273
Mihoshi, stop hallucinating!

00:14:20.273 --> 00:14:22.942
Now, you are a galaxy police detective.

00:14:22.942 --> 00:14:24.967
Will you get a grip... Huh?

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:50.995
Now, one bite for each, all right?

00:15:06.319 --> 00:15:08.254
Thank you very much for waiting.

00:15:08.254 --> 00:15:12.491
A luxury hotel and delicious food.

00:15:12.491 --> 00:15:16.587
And a beautiful woman.

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.495
What is it?

00:15:24.604 --> 00:15:26.973
Oh, I forgot!

00:15:26.973 --> 00:15:28.838
Well, they can wait.

00:15:33.179 --> 00:15:35.915
All right, enough already.

00:15:35.915 --> 00:15:37.817
Time to go back.

00:15:37.817 --> 00:15:40.581
Here. That should be enough, I think.

00:15:43.089 --> 00:15:45.080
Thank you very much, Ma'am.

00:16:02.141 --> 00:16:03.809
And around the stretch they come.

00:16:03.809 --> 00:16:07.880
Mayo-dan is in the lead,
followed closely by Winning Kid.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:10.576
- Come on, let's go!
- All right! Go! Go! Go!

00:16:13.119 --> 00:16:15.417
All right! Go! Go!

00:16:16.255 --> 00:16:17.722
Come on...

00:16:18.457 --> 00:16:22.928
Closing in fast from the outside
crossing the finish line is number 37,

00:16:22.928 --> 00:16:25.765
one minute and 29 seconds.

00:16:25.765 --> 00:16:30.269
Oh, no... I lost.

00:16:30.269 --> 00:16:32.737
I really cannot believe this!

00:16:41.714 --> 00:16:43.739
Are you hungry?

00:16:46.018 --> 00:16:48.788
Oh, I know.

00:16:48.788 --> 00:16:53.459
Ah, yes, I wonder how
those guys are doing also.

00:16:53.459 --> 00:16:55.359
Tenchi...

00:16:56.929 --> 00:16:58.954
Bank of Jurai, huh?

00:17:03.035 --> 00:17:05.871
Oh, Ryoko...

00:17:05.871 --> 00:17:11.043
We shouldn't have trusted Ryoko.

00:17:11.043 --> 00:17:12.912
What now, Tenchi?

00:17:12.912 --> 00:17:16.315
Hey, now, don't you worry.
She'll be here soon. Just trust me.

00:17:16.315 --> 00:17:17.950
But, Tenchi...

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:18.918
It's going to be all right.

00:17:18.918 --> 00:17:24.323
You know, Sasami, back
on Earth we have a fable.

00:17:24.323 --> 00:17:29.095
It is the story of two friends and the
story's moral is that if you trust someone...

00:17:29.095 --> 00:17:33.232
Yeah! If you trust someone...
your faith will be rewarded.

00:17:33.232 --> 00:17:37.828
Yeah, but Ryoko is a space pirate and all.

00:17:46.312 --> 00:17:49.213
This should be more
than enough money, I think.

00:18:13.906 --> 00:18:16.308
Okay. There they are.

00:18:16.308 --> 00:18:17.798
Ryo-Ohki.

00:18:23.716 --> 00:18:27.920
Oh, look! She's on the roof!
Look out! Oh, it's the space pirate.

00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:30.286
Let's get out of here, Ryo-Ohki.

00:18:41.066 --> 00:18:44.670
The repairs are finished finally.

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:46.005
Washu?

00:18:46.005 --> 00:18:48.707
Can we go now?

00:18:48.707 --> 00:18:51.243
Can we go to a planet where we
can get something to eat now, please?

00:18:51.243 --> 00:18:53.446
But Ryoko isn't here yet.

00:18:53.446 --> 00:18:56.482
Let's just forget about that traitor, all right?

00:18:56.482 --> 00:18:59.042
Oh, look, Ayeka.

00:19:03.189 --> 00:19:05.991
Hi, guys. I'm back.

00:19:05.991 --> 00:19:08.118
I would like to thank you
for waiting for me so patiently.

00:19:10.729 --> 00:19:14.266
Oh, Tenchi, you missed me, didn't you?

00:19:14.266 --> 00:19:15.668
Ayeka, get me some tea.

00:19:15.668 --> 00:19:19.638
Who do you think you are?
And what took you so long, Ryoko?

00:19:19.638 --> 00:19:21.128
Here.

00:19:24.343 --> 00:19:27.246
I'm sorry. Everything took
a little longer than I thought.

00:19:27.246 --> 00:19:32.017
See? My flower told me the truth.

00:19:32.017 --> 00:19:34.451
Yeah. You must've gotten sidetracked.

00:19:35.588 --> 00:19:38.691
Please don't concern
yourself with the minor details.

00:19:38.691 --> 00:19:41.126
You were so right, Tenchi.

00:19:41.126 --> 00:19:44.230
Our trust was truly rewarded.

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:46.165
Yup, that's right.

00:19:46.165 --> 00:19:48.734
Come on, let's fix something to eat.

00:19:48.734 --> 00:19:50.269
Yeah, let's have a feast!

00:19:50.269 --> 00:19:52.464
- All right!
- Yeah!

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:03.839
What's going on this time?

00:20:13.726 --> 00:20:16.028
Why, it's all money!

00:20:16.028 --> 00:20:20.666
With this much money we can go in
any restaurants we want, I guarantee you.

00:20:20.666 --> 00:20:23.202
Ryoko... you didn't... did you?

00:20:23.202 --> 00:20:27.006
The bank I robbed was the Bank of
Jurai, so there's nothing to worry about.

00:20:27.006 --> 00:20:28.641
The Bank of Jurai?

00:20:28.641 --> 00:20:30.309
The money in the Bank of
Jurai is my people's money!

00:20:30.309 --> 00:20:33.176
Don't you understand anything, Ryoko?

00:20:44.423 --> 00:20:48.294
Oh! We're even involved in a bank robbery!

00:20:48.294 --> 00:20:51.397
Tenchi, our trust was not rewarded.

00:20:51.397 --> 00:20:53.160
That's right.

00:20:55.734 --> 00:20:57.603
I'm so hungry.

00:20:57.603 --> 00:21:00.005
Yeah. Me, too.

00:21:00.005 --> 00:21:04.738
I'm starving...

00:22:55.354 --> 00:22:59.058
We wander into the Sargasso Sea
in space and encounter a ghost ship!

00:22:59.058 --> 00:23:02.061
Sasami disappears when a
mysterious girl invites her to the ship!

00:23:02.061 --> 00:23:04.797
- W-What shall we do?
- Rescue Sasami now!

00:23:04.797 --> 00:23:07.800
- You mean, go into that ghost ship?
- Of course! Where else?

00:23:07.800 --> 00:23:09.702
Well, I wish you good luck.

00:23:09.702 --> 00:23:11.170
You're coming with us, Mihoshi!

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:12.905
I was afraid you'd say that.

00:23:12.905 --> 00:23:16.241
A sweet friendship is formed
between Sasami and the girl.

00:23:16.241 --> 00:23:18.444
Next episode is: "No Need for a Ghost!"

00:23:18.444 --> 00:23:20.546
A story of a time of life
young girls cherish forever.

00:23:20.546 --> 00:23:22.810
It's unquestionably sweet!
